   "find": "<figure class=\"lcp\"><p class=\"kick\">Diagnostic workup</p><div class=\"ttl\"><span><b class=\"step\">1</b>Is it glomerular? If not, does a symptom name the cause?</span></div><ol class=\"path\"><li class=\"pt\"><span class=\"when\">First</span><div class=\"tile first\"><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Urinalysis with microscopy</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Dipstick blood, 3 or more red cells per high-power field (hpf)</b><span class=\"mask\">True hematuria</span></p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Dipstick blood, no red cells</b><span class=\"mask\">Suggests myoglobin or hemoglobin</span></p></div></div></li><li class=\"pt\"><span class=\"when\">By branch</span><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Urine culture</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Dysuria, leukocyte esterase and pyuria with growth</b><span class=\"mask\">Cystitis: treat, repeat the urinalysis after antibiotics; image only if blood persists</span></p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Dysuria and pyuria with no growth, in a sexually active adolescent</b><span class=\"mask\">Chlamydia and gonorrhea nucleic acid amplification test (NAAT)</span></p></div><i class=\"plus\" aria-label=\"and\"></i><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Urine sediment: casts and red cell shape</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Red cell casts, dysmorphic red cells, protein</b><span class=\"mask\">Creatinine, complement levels, CBC, blood pressure; antistreptolysin O (ASO) after strep</span></p></div><i class=\"plus\" aria-label=\"and\"></i><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Contrast computed tomography (CT) of the abdomen</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Renal injury</b><span class=\"mask\">Hematuria after abdominal or flank trauma</span></p></div><i class=\"plus\" aria-label=\"and\"></i><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Renal ultrasound</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Flank pain with crystals</b><span class=\"mask\">Stone: the first image in a child with flank pain, no radiation</span></p></div><i class=\"plus\" aria-label=\"and\"></i><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\